1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,975
Eight Maven lessons. Today is the proof.

2
00:00:03,525 --> 00:00:04,494
Not a new tool.

3
00:00:04,494 --> 00:00:05,335
One real job,

4
00:00:05,335 --> 00:00:08,114
from a broken project to a published build,

5
00:00:08,114 --> 00:00:09,989
using everything you learned.

6
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:12,392
Cart core does not compile.

7
00:00:12,392 --> 00:00:13,284
A test fails.

8
00:00:13,284 --> 00:00:16,030
The jar changes every time you build it.

9
00:00:16,030 --> 00:00:18,158
And it must reach a real Nexus,

10
00:00:18,158 --> 00:00:19,051
with a login.

11
00:00:19,601 --> 00:00:24,294
You will watch me do it, live, then you do it alone, and a checker judges your result.

12
00:00:24,844 --> 00:00:25,868
One honest note.

13
00:00:25,868 --> 00:00:28,236
The three problems are planted by me,

14
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:28,876
the build,

15
00:00:28,876 --> 00:00:31,628
the repository and the checks are all real.

16
00:00:33,178 --> 00:00:38,255
This is the mastery evidence for the Maven domain. Six skills, in one scenario.

17
00:00:38,805 --> 00:00:42,219
Read a failed build, and name the cause. Lesson ninety-two.

18
00:00:42,769 --> 00:00:47,782
Inspect the dependency tree, and fix a version. Lessons eighty-nine and ninety-one.

19
00:00:48,332 --> 00:00:52,513
Run the lifecycle, and let a test prove the code. Lesson eighty-six.

20
00:00:53,063 --> 00:00:58,589
Make the build reproducible, so the same input gives the same jar. Lesson eighty-seven.

21
00:00:59,139 --> 00:01:01,290
Publish to a repository manager,

22
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:03,778
with the password outside every file.

23
00:01:03,778 --> 00:01:05,795
Lessons ninety and ninety-one.

24
00:01:06,345 --> 00:01:10,163
And document it: what you did, what went wrong, and how you clean up.

25
00:01:12,213 --> 00:01:18,592
Go into the project. Type: CD, slash opt, slash lab ninety-four, slash cart dash core.

26
00:01:19,142 --> 00:01:20,421
Put the Nexus password in a variable,

27
00:01:20,421 --> 00:01:21,147
from the locked file.

28
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:22,911
Type: export C O R P underscore PASS equals dollar,

29
00:01:22,911 --> 00:01:23,326
parenthesis,

30
00:01:23,326 --> 00:01:23,464
cat,

31
00:01:23,464 --> 00:01:23,741
dot dot,

32
00:01:23,741 --> 00:01:24,432
slash pass dot text.

33
00:01:24,982 --> 00:01:27,052
List the folder. Type: L S.

34
00:01:27,602 --> 00:01:31,740
A pom, a settings file, and the source. This is the project we ship.

35
00:01:32,290 --> 00:01:32,795
Step one.

36
00:01:32,795 --> 00:01:33,300
Build it,

37
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,096
and show only the compile error.

38
00:01:35,096 --> 00:01:35,770
Type: M V N,

39
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:36,162
dash B,

40
00:01:36,162 --> 00:01:36,948
clean package,

41
00:01:36,948 --> 00:01:37,453
and grep.

42
00:01:39,703 --> 00:01:42,796
Maven resolves the dependencies, then compiles.

43
00:01:48,346 --> 00:01:49,635
Cannot find symbol.

44
00:01:49,635 --> 00:01:51,330
A method called truncate.

45
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:52,482
The code is fine.

46
00:01:52,482 --> 00:01:55,194
The library we asked for may be too old.

47
00:01:55,744 --> 00:01:56,802
Look at the dependency tree,

48
00:01:56,802 --> 00:01:58,123
and keep the line about lang three.

49
00:01:58,123 --> 00:01:58,576
Type: M V N,

50
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,407
dependency colon tree,

51
00:01:59,407 --> 00:02:00,011
and grep dash O.

52
00:02:02,161 --> 00:02:03,351
Commons lang three,

53
00:02:03,351 --> 00:02:04,916
version three point four.

54
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:06,356
Truncate arrived later.

55
00:02:06,356 --> 00:02:07,921
The cause is the version.

56
00:02:08,471 --> 00:02:09,401
Fix the cause,

57
00:02:09,401 --> 00:02:09,998
with sed.

58
00:02:09,998 --> 00:02:12,056
Three point four becomes three,

59
00:02:12,056 --> 00:02:12,654
fourteen,

60
00:02:12,654 --> 00:02:12,986
zero.

61
00:02:12,986 --> 00:02:14,380
The dependency stays.

62
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:20,309
Build again, and keep the line that compares the two values.

63
00:02:20,859 --> 00:02:23,056
It compiles now. Then the tests run.

64
00:02:29,606 --> 00:02:30,584
Expected Cloud,

65
00:02:30,584 --> 00:02:31,430
but was Clou.

66
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:33,776
We moved forward: the code compiles,

67
00:02:33,776 --> 00:02:35,665
and a test proves a real bug.

68
00:02:36,215 --> 00:02:40,482
Fix the code, not the test. The code cuts four letters. It should cut five.

69
00:02:42,732 --> 00:02:45,910
Build once more, and keep the test summary and the build line.

70
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:50,298
The tests run again.

71
00:02:56,848 --> 00:02:57,550
Tests run,

72
00:02:57,550 --> 00:02:57,830
one.

73
00:02:57,830 --> 00:02:58,462
Failures,

74
00:02:58,462 --> 00:02:58,813
zero.

75
00:02:58,813 --> 00:02:59,796
Build success.

76
00:02:59,796 --> 00:03:01,130
The tests prove it,

77
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:02,885
and we never skipped one.

78
00:03:03,435 --> 00:03:03,672
Next,

79
00:03:03,672 --> 00:03:04,526
a harder question.

80
00:03:04,526 --> 00:03:05,807
Is this build reproducible?

81
00:03:05,807 --> 00:03:06,377
Build twice,

82
00:03:06,377 --> 00:03:09,366
and print the first sixteen letters of the checksum of the jar.

83
00:03:13,316 --> 00:03:15,086
Two builds, two seconds apart.

84
00:03:29,636 --> 00:03:31,035
Two different checksums,

85
00:03:31,035 --> 00:03:32,258
from the same source.

86
00:03:32,258 --> 00:03:34,589
Maven put the build time inside the jar.

87
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:36,570
You cannot prove what you shipped.

88
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,854
Fix it with one property: the output timestamp.

89
00:03:39,854 --> 00:03:40,611
A fixed date.

90
00:03:40,611 --> 00:03:41,192
Type: sed,

91
00:03:41,192 --> 00:03:42,880
and add it to the properties.

92
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:51,294
Same test again. Build twice, and print the checksums.

93
00:03:57,944 --> 00:03:59,714
Two builds, two seconds apart.

94
00:04:14,264 --> 00:04:19,470
The same checksum twice. Same input, same jar. That is a reproducible build.

95
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:25,246
Now publish. Build with the settings file, and keep only the name of the uploaded jar.

96
00:04:29,296 --> 00:04:33,499
Maven builds, and uploads to Nexus with the login from the variable.

97
00:04:44,049 --> 00:04:47,206
Uploaded. A snapshot of cart core, with its build number.

98
00:04:47,756 --> 00:04:52,322
Prove it from the server. Ask Nexus how many jars corp snapshots holds.

99
00:05:00,572 --> 00:05:02,684
One. The server says it has our jar.

100
00:05:03,234 --> 00:05:03,887
Last proof.

101
00:05:03,887 --> 00:05:06,561
Does the password appear in any project file?

102
00:05:06,561 --> 00:05:08,759
Count it in the pom and the settings.

103
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:14,621
Zero in both. The password lived only in the environment. That is how you ship safely.

104
00:05:16,171 --> 00:05:19,606
Your mastery task. The same journey, on your own project.

105
00:05:20,156 --> 00:05:24,550
One: build it, read the first error, and fix the cause. Keep the dependency.

106
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:29,708
Two: fix the code so the test passes. Do not edit the test, and do not skip it.

107
00:05:30,258 --> 00:05:34,248
Three: make the build reproducible. Two builds, the same checksum.

108
00:05:34,798 --> 00:05:38,403
Four: publish to Nexus. The password stays in the variable.

109
00:05:38,953 --> 00:05:43,753
Five: write report dot text. Result, trouble, and cleanup, in three lines.

110
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:50,006
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

111
00:05:50,556 --> 00:05:52,255
The lab lives on git hub,

112
00:05:52,255 --> 00:05:53,410
at it dash waves,

113
00:05:53,410 --> 00:05:54,973
slash dev ops dash A I,

114
00:05:54,973 --> 00:05:56,468
in the folder academy,

115
00:05:56,468 --> 00:05:57,148
slash lab.

116
00:05:57,698 --> 00:06:02,732
Two files: lab ninety-four dot S H, and shortcuts ninety-four dot S H.

117
00:06:03,282 --> 00:06:04,152
Install it,

118
00:06:04,152 --> 00:06:07,708
in your Ubuntu virtual machine: sudo install,

119
00:06:07,708 --> 00:06:09,525
dash m seven five five,

120
00:06:09,525 --> 00:06:11,422
lab ninety-four dot S H,

121
00:06:11,422 --> 00:06:12,607
into slash usr,

122
00:06:12,607 --> 00:06:13,555
slash local,

123
00:06:13,555 --> 00:06:14,504
slash S bin.

124
00:06:15,054 --> 00:06:19,218
Load the short name with: source shortcuts ninety-four dot S H.

125
00:06:19,218 --> 00:06:20,936
Then you can type: lab up,

126
00:06:20,936 --> 00:06:21,597
lab check,

127
00:06:21,597 --> 00:06:22,456
and lab down.

128
00:06:23,006 --> 00:06:24,190
You need a J D K,

129
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:24,608
Maven,

130
00:06:24,608 --> 00:06:26,141
curl and python three,

131
00:06:26,141 --> 00:06:28,370
about three gigabytes of memory,

132
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:30,250
and an internet connection.

133
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:32,549
The first lab up downloads Nexus,

134
00:06:32,549 --> 00:06:34,569
about five hundred megabytes.

135
00:06:35,119 --> 00:06:40,538
Lab down stops Nexus and removes everything. Only run it in your own virtual machine.

136
00:06:42,588 --> 00:06:44,657
Pass or fail. You need all six.

137
00:06:45,207 --> 00:06:47,021
Five pass lines in lab check.

138
00:06:47,571 --> 00:06:50,216
You fixed the cause every time, never a symptom.

139
00:06:50,766 --> 00:06:53,689
No skip tests, and the test file is untouched.

140
00:06:54,239 --> 00:06:55,988
Two builds give the same checksum.

141
00:06:56,538 --> 00:06:58,138
The password is in no file.

142
00:06:58,688 --> 00:07:02,933
Report dot text tells the story, and lab down leaves nothing behind.

143
00:07:03,483 --> 00:07:04,785
To pass, all six.

144
00:07:06,835 --> 00:07:09,672
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

145
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:12,313
One: lab up, and read the task file.

146
00:07:12,863 --> 00:07:15,338
Two: build, and read only the first error.

147
00:07:15,888 --> 00:07:19,130
Three: fix the version, then the code, then the timestamp.

148
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,835
Four: deploy, and check it in Nexus.

149
00:07:22,385 --> 00:07:25,158
Five: write report dot text, and lab check.

150
00:07:25,708 --> 00:07:28,290
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

151
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,674
Pause the video, and begin now.

152
00:07:46,224 --> 00:07:47,099
Quick check.

153
00:07:47,649 --> 00:07:50,934
Which tool shows you the version of a library you did not choose?

154
00:07:51,484 --> 00:07:53,575
Why must the build be reproducible?

155
00:07:54,125 --> 00:07:55,554
Where does the password live?

156
00:07:56,104 --> 00:07:57,491
What goes in the report?

157
00:07:58,041 --> 00:08:01,070
Domain mastery covered: M C ten, Maven.

158
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,689
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

159
00:08:14,239 --> 00:08:16,778
Next: Gradle, the other big build tool.

160
00:08:17,328 --> 00:08:20,656
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
